sys/cdefs.h, mach/arm/vm_param.h: select XNU_PLATFORM_MacOSX.

xnu's published headers carry the settings for EVERY Apple product, each
guarded by `#ifdef XNU_PLATFORM_<name>`.  Apple's header-install step resolves
them with unifdef -- Libc/xcodescripts/headers.sh:407 runs the same tool for
the same reason -- so the SDK copy contains one product's block and no #ifdef.
Nothing in a published tree does that for us, and with no XNU_PLATFORM_ defined
the results are silently wrong rather than loud:

  sys/cdefs.h        __DARWIN_ONLY_UNIX_CONFORMANCE is left UNDEFINED, so
                     __DARWIN_SUF_UNIX03 becomes "$UNIX2003" and every
                     __DARWIN_ALIAS'd libc function is renamed.  Measured on
                     libobjc.A.dylib: 7 undefined symbols that no dylib on
                     earth exports here -- _open$UNIX2003, _close$UNIX2003,
                     _write$UNIX2003, _fsync$UNIX2003, _pread$UNIX2003,
                     _nanosleep$UNIX2003, _strerror$UNIX2003.  On arm64 macOS
                     the correct value is 1 and the suffix is empty.

  mach/arm/vm_param.h  MACH_VM_MAX_ADDRESS_RAW falls to the embedded value
                     0x0000000FC0000000 (64 GB) instead of macOS's
                     0x00007FFFFE000000 (128 TB).  Nothing would have failed
                     to compile; the number would just have been wrong, which
                     is precisely the risk docs/SDK_SURVEY.md §6.1 named.

The selection is written into the headers rather than passed as -D so that it
cannot be forgotten by a guest build.  An iOS sysroot would be a differently
staged tree, not a different command line.

--- a/sys/cdefs.h
+++ b/sys/cdefs.h
@@ -25,6 +25,18 @@
  *
  * @APPLE_OSREFERENCE_LICENSE_HEADER_END@
  */
+
+/* machorun: sdk/patches/0002-xnu-platform-macosx.patch -- select the product.
+ * xnu's published headers gate per-product settings on XNU_PLATFORM_<name>,
+ * which Apple's header-install step resolves with unifdef.  sdk/ IS the macOS
+ * sysroot, so it selects MacOSX here, in the header, where it cannot be
+ * forgotten on a command line. */
+#if !defined(XNU_PLATFORM_MacOSX) && !defined(XNU_PLATFORM_iPhoneOS) && \
+    !defined(XNU_PLATFORM_iPhoneSimulator) && !defined(XNU_PLATFORM_AppleTVOS) && \
+    !defined(XNU_PLATFORM_WatchOS) && !defined(XNU_PLATFORM_BridgeOS) && \
+    !defined(XNU_PLATFORM_DriverKit) && !defined(XNU_PLATFORM_XROS)
+#define XNU_PLATFORM_MacOSX 1
+#endif
